            <ArticleTitle>Commentary on headache currents articles by Alhazzani and Goddeau.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1028-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Headache is a symptom of cerebrovascular disease, particularly the hemorrhagic type. Also, certain headache types, notably migraine with aura, predispose individuals to ischemic and perhaps hemorrhagic stroke. The relationship between migraine and cerebrovascular disease can be causal, coincidental or co-morbid.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
